# The corpus never enters the image (10.3.12.1): it is a versioned external asset read by
# the catalog build and by nothing else, and an image that shipped whatever happened to be
# on someone's disk would not be reproducible from the repository.
data/

# The one exception, and the reason the rule above is not simply `data/`: the catalog
# document *is* a build input (8.11.1).  It is generated rather than committed, so it can
# only reach the image through the build context, and an un-negated `data/` would exclude
# it and fail the `COPY` in the Dockerfile.
!data/catalog/strategy-catalog.json

.venv/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
project_metadata/plans/
